# Whitelist, not a blacklist.
#
# Everything here is ignored unless it is named below. That way a new file
# Claude Code drops into this directory -- a cache, a session transcript, a
# credential -- stays out of the repository by default rather than by my
# remembering to add it.
#
# Deliberately NOT tracked, and why:
#   .credentials.json   an OAuth token, bound to this machine. Run `claude
#                       login` on the other one instead.
#   ../.claude.json     machineID, userID, project history with local paths.
#   plugins/            re-installed from the marketplace on demand.
#   cache/ sessions/ shell-snapshots/ file-history/ backups/ ide/ session-env/
#                       state belonging to one machine.
#   projects/*/*.jsonl  full session transcripts. Private, large, useless
#                       elsewhere.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/settings.json
!/rules/
!/skills/
!/agents/

# Memory, and only memory -- descend into projects/<name>/memory/ while
# leaving the transcripts sitting beside it ignored.
!/projects/
/projects/*
!/projects/*/
/projects/*/*
!/projects/*/memory/

# Documentation for this repo itself.
!/README.md
!/.gitattributes
